{"author":{"id":"694fb8161bd8bf91df2a28db7c649e48f8c5fa47ad3ad0234607d35f0482801a"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1789910547,"nonce":"fW5nrGIm8oPeMQFnSRXDvwAaBp8=","message":"Re-evaluated and removed in c0c8dcbf4ac3cb3fbf232252e535a9e22aa9d820. With WLIFT_ENABLE_IC_JIT=1 the LLVM e2e suite passed but hatch-fsm failed deterministically: the fast path never drained an error the compiled callee raised (a Fiber.abort inside the callee ran on). Beyond that it entered the callee without the JitContext the slow path sets (closure, defining class, module vars), and under Cranelift jit_leaf is true for every compiled body, so the 'leaf' gate no longer restricted it. Measured with the drain fixed: method_call, ash/method_call, delta_blue, dyn_dispatch, binary_trees all within noise, because once callers are compiled they call directly and the interpreter's site only runs during warmup. So the path is gone, along with WLIFT_ENABLE_IC_JIT and WLIFT_TRACE_IC_JIT; kind=1 entries are still recorded for the compiler's devirtualisation, and the threaded interpreter's own kind=1 dispatch (default on, WLIFT_DISABLE_IC_JIT) is untouched.","files":null}]}